{"path":"memory/polymorphic_allocator/delete_object","title":"std::pmr::polymorphic_allocator<T>::delete_object","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::pmr::polymorphic_allocator&lt;T&gt;::</span>delete_object","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/memory/polymorphic_allocator/delete_object","section":"memory","kind":"page","summary":"Destroys the object of type U and deallocates storage allocated for it.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> U <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><span class=\"kw4\">void</span> delete_object<span class=\"br0\">(</span> U<span class=\"sy2\">*</span> p <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Destroys the object of type <code>U</code> and deallocates storage allocated for it.\n</p><p>Equivalent to<br>\n<code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/allocator_traits\"><span class=\"kw705\">std::<span class=\"me2\">allocator_traits</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>polymorphic_allocator<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">destroy</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this, p<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span><br>\ndeallocate_object<span class=\"br0\">(</span>p<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></code>\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> p\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> pointer to the object to destroy and deallocate\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\n<p>Throws nothing.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>This function was introduced for use with the fully-specialized allocator <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/polymorphic_allocator\"><span class=\"kw711\">std::<span class=\"me2\">pmr</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">polymorphic_allocator</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&gt;</span></span></code>, but it may be useful in any specialization.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/polymorphic_allocator/deallocate_bytes\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>deallocate_bytes</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  free raw memory obtained from <code>allocate_bytes</code> <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/polymorphic_allocator/deallocate_object\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>deallocate_object</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  frees raw memory obtained by <code>allocate_object</code> <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/allocator_traits/deallocate\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>deallocate</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-cmark\">[static]</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  deallocates storage using the allocator <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public static member function of <code>std::allocator_traits&lt;Alloc&gt;</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/memory_resource/deallocate\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>deallocate</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  deallocates memory <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function of <code>std::pmr::memory_resource</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"memory","title":"Memory management library"},{"path":"memory/polymorphic_allocator","title":"std::pmr::polymorphic_allocator"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::pmr::polymorphic_allocator<T>::delete_object","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++20. Destroys the object of type U and deallocates storage allocated for it."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"p"},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"Throws nothing."},{"label":"Notes","note":"This function was introduced for use with the fully-specialized allocator std::pmr::polymorphic_allocator<>, but it may be useful in any specialization."},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"deallocate_bytes","note":"free raw memory obtained from allocate_bytes"},{"label":"deallocate_object","note":"frees raw memory obtained by allocate_object"},{"label":"deallocate","note":"deallocates storage using the allocator"},{"label":"deallocate","note":"deallocates memory"}]}]},"standards":["C++20"],"wordCount":103,"codeBlockCount":0}
